  "examples": [
    {
      "coptic": "ⲟⲩⲟϩ ϩⲟⲧⲉ ⲉⲧⲁϥϣⲁⲓ ⲛϫⲉⲫⲣⲏ ⲁϥⲉⲣⲕⲁⲩⲙⲁ ⲟⲩⲟϩ ⲉⲑⲃⲉϫⲉⲙⲙⲟⲛⲧⲉϥ ⲛⲟⲩⲛⲓ ⲁϥ**ϣⲱⲟⲩⲓ**",
      "english": "When the sun had risen, it was scorched; and because it had no root, it withered away.",
      "source": "Bohairic Gospel of Mark 4 (Digital Edition)",
      "urn": "urn:cts:copticLit:nt.mark.bohairic_ed:4",
      "dialect": "bohairic"
    },
    {
      "coptic": "ⲧⲉⲛⲟⲩ ⲇⲉ ⲁⲓ**ϣⲟⲟⲩⲉ** ⲁⲩⲱ ⲁⲓⲥⲣⲟϥⲣϥ ·",
      "english": "but now I am dried up and withered.",
      "source": "History of Eustathius and Theopiste part 1",
      "urn": "urn:cts:copticLit:lives.eustathius.budge:1-30",
      "dialect": "sahidic"
    },
    {
      "coptic": "ϧⲉⲛⲛⲁⲓ ⲁⲡⲉϥⲥⲱⲙⲁ **ϣⲱⲟⲩⲓ** ⲟⲩⲟϩ ⲁⲡⲉϥϣⲁⲣ ⲧⲱⲙⲓ ⲉⲛⲉϥⲕⲁⲥ ⲉⲁϥϣⲙⲁ ⲉⲙⲁϣⲱ ⲟⲩⲟϩ ⲡⲉϥⲃⲓⲟⲥ ⲧⲏⲣϥ ⲛⲉⲙⲡⲉϥⲥⲕⲟⲡⲟⲥ ⲛⲁϥⲧⲉⲛⲑⲱⲛⲧ ⲉⲏⲗⲓⲁⲥ ⲡⲓⲑⲉⲥⲃⲩⲧⲏⲥ ⲡⲓⲉⲛⲓⲱⲭⲟⲥ ⲛⲧⲉⲡⲓⲥⲣⲁⲏⲗ .",
      "english": "As a result, his body became emaciated—his skin taut and clinging to his bones. Shenoute modeled his entire life and purpose after Elijah the Tishbite, the charioteer of Israel.",
      "source": "Life of Shenoute - part 1",
      "urn": "urn:cts:copticLit:lives.boh_shenoute.leipoldt_ed:1-26",
      "dialect": "bohairic"
    },
    {
      "coptic": "ⲁⲩⲱ ⲛⲧⲉⲣⲉⲡⲣⲏ ϣⲁ ⲁⲩϩⲱϭⲃ ⲁⲩⲱ ⲉⲧⲃⲉ ϫⲉⲙⲡⲟⲩϫⲉⲛⲟⲩⲛⲉ ⲉⲃⲟⲗ ⲁⲩ**ϣⲟⲟⲩⲉ**",
      "english": "When the sun had risen, it was scorched; and because it had no root, it withered away.",
